-- title:
--   Factorisation of a supersingular attachment through the Gauss residue field
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K_2$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L((q))$ obtained by base change, i.e. generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios of $\Gamma_0(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K_2$ compatible with $L$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j_2 \in K_2$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion the image of $j(q)$, and write $A_2 =$ `chartAlgFin A K₂ j₂` for the subalgebra of elements of $K_2$ integral over $A[j_2]$. Let $W_2$ be a valuation subring of $K_2$ consisting exactly of those $f$ admitting power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f \hat y = \hat x$ in $L((q))$, and assume $A_2 \subseteq W_2$. Let $b_M \in A_2$ have $q$-expansion the image of $j(q^M)$. Assume a ring isomorphism $\varepsilon_2$ from the residue field of $W_2$ onto [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A) M`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L61), the subfield of $\kappa(A)((q))$ generated over $\kappa(A)$ by $\tilde\jmath$ and $\tilde\jmath_M$, carrying the residue of $j_2$ to `jGeomGen`, the residue of $b_M$ to `jNGeomGen`, and the residue of each $a \in A$ to its image in $\kappa(A)$. Let $\mathfrak{y}_2$ be an ideal of $A_2$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ in which every element satisfies $x^{p^n} = x$ for some $n > 0$, let $w$ be a place of [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC k M`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L61) over $k$ lying in [`ModularCurve.ssPlaces p M k`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularNodePlaces.html#L113), and let $\rho : A_2 \to$ [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC k M`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L61) be a ring homomorphism with $\rho(\varpi) = 0$, $\rho(j_2) =$ `jGeomGen k M`, with image inside the valuation subring of $w$, with $\rho(b)$ a nonunit of that subring exactly when $b \in \mathfrak{y}_2$, and such that every $f$ in the target is a quotient $f = a/b$ with $a, b$ in the $k$-subalgebra generated by the range of $\rho$ and $b \ne 0$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\tilde\theta$ from the residue field of $W_2$ to [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC k M`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L61) with $\tilde\theta(\bar b) = \rho(b)$ for every $b \in A_2$.
--
--   This is the factorisation step for an attachment map at a supersingular point: an arbitrary ring homomorphism $\rho$ out of the $j$-finite chart ring of the two-chart integral model of $X_0(Mp)$, centred at the chart ideal and birational onto the characteristic-$p$ modular function field, is shown to descend through the residue field of the Gauss valuation ring, so that it can subsequently be compared with the canonical coefficient-change map. It is used in the computation identifying the width of a supersingular node with the order of the inertia group, via the identification of $\ker \rho$ with $A_2 \cap \mathfrak{m}_{W_2}$ provided by [`ModularCurve.XZeroPM.mem_ker_iff_coe_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_of_map_jChartFin_eq_jGeomGen_gamma0_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XZeroPM.mem_ker_iff_coe_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_of_map_jChartFin_eq_jGeomGen_gamma0_mul).
